WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.119
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will set up voice channels

00:00:05.119 --> 00:00:10.237
for team coordination. Field teams need the correct channel membership and working device

00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:15.356
audio before an exercise or deployment. We will explain the features, the setup

00:00:15.356 --> 00:00:18.900
decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.926
A search team uses its team channel during a training exercise. Coordinate field

00:00:24.926 --> 00:00:30.351
teams through app-based voice channels. The examples in this series use a fictional

00:00:30.351 --> 00:00:33.690
department and are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:40.308
Voice. Push-to-Talk voice channels. Create channels and add the members who use them.

00:00:40.308 --> 00:00:45.400
Availability also depends on PTT. Check access in the target department.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.500
Push-to-Talk. The Push-to-Talk add-on: voice channels in the Resgrid apps. Review seats, supported

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:59.000
clients and channel setup. PTT does not provide phone dispatch alerts or certify

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.500
radio replacement. Availability also depends on PTT. Check access in the target department.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:12.166
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Confirm Push-to-Talk access

00:01:12.166 --> 00:01:18.231
and supported clients. Step 2. Create a training channel and add its intended

00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:24.297
members. Step 3. Join from two demo devices and verify transmit, receive, and

00:01:24.297 --> 00:01:25.230
microphone permissions.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:31.605
Now verify the result. Check membership and actual audio in both directions on

00:01:31.605 --> 00:01:37.380
the devices used. Review channel access after membership changes. A common problem to

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:43.156
watch for: Push-to-Talk channel setup is separate from phone voice alerts and audio-stream

00:01:43.156 --> 00:01:43.600
configuration.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.155
Your practice task is simple. Run a two-device training-channel check and record which

00:01:49.155 --> 00:01:54.111
members can transmit and receive. Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and

00:01:54.111 --> 00:01:59.066
when it should be reviewed. Use the linked feature scripts for the detailed

00:01:59.066 --> 00:02:00.210
screen recording plan.

